SDK UI: let the app give the main window an initial position and size before it is first shown.
Phase B item B5 (docs/sdk-from-source.md). Applied by tools/build_sdk_from_source.py
(SDK_BEHAVIOUR_PATCHES). WindowSDL::OpenImpl creates the window hidden and shows it
inside ReXApp::SetupPresentation, at SDL's default centred position, before the app
gets control, so a restored position made the window appear centred and then jump.
Adds Window::SetInitialPosition and Window::SetInitialSize (applied while hidden: the
size is clamped to 640x360 .. the usable display area, the position keeps the title bar
on a connected display; the `monitor` cvar takes priority over the position; under
fullscreen they become the windowed frame that leaving fullscreen returns to), the
ReXApp::OnPreOpenWindow hook, and the REX_UI_WINDOW_INITIAL_POSITION /
REX_UI_WINDOW_INITIAL_SIZE feature macros. The new Window members are appended last,
so the member offsets that other modules compiled against the unpatched header (the
Metal plugin) see are unchanged.
The executable's SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_SHOWN watch (src/core/fable2_window_position.cpp)
stands down when the macro is present; it stays the fallback on the prebuilt runtime.

